---
source: crates/acpilot-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&ext)
---
Install, verify, and approve extensions

Usage: acpilot ext [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add           Install an extension from a local directory
  import-theme  Import a TextMate `.tmTheme` as a theme extension and install it
  verify        Rehash every installed version and report any that are blocked
  prune         Remove versions no profile activates
  activate      Approve an installed extension for one profile
  deactivate    Withdraw approval from one profile
  why           Explain how a preset or agent resolves for one profile
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <NAME|DIR>
          Profile name, or a profile directory.
          
          Accepted before or after the subcommand, because every verb that has an opinion about
          identity reads one choice. A single segment is a profile name under `<config>/profiles`; a
          path opens that directory. `tui` and `serve` use it only when they start the daemon: a
          daemon already running keeps the profile it was started with, and naming a different one
          there is an error rather than a silent mismatch. A name that does not resolve is an error,
          never a quieter fallback: guessing sends a work prompt with a personal key.
          
          [env: ACPILOT_PROFILE=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
